# OCTOFIT SDLC (Cursor)

- This project uses **Cursor agents/skills/hooks**.
- Before a new story: read `octofit.json`. Start new work only if prior stages are `succeed`. If any stage is `failed` or `in-progress`, resume via `@master-sdlc-flow`.
- New story entrypoint: `@master-sdlc-flow`.
- Store phase outputs under `artifacts/<JIRA-KEY>/` with exact names: `requirements.md`, `architecture.md`, `design-review.md`, `impl-plan.md`, `implementation.md`, `review.md`, `verify.md`, `pr.md`.
- Update `octofit.json` stage status after each phase (`succeed` | `failed` | `in-progress`).
- Prefer Atlassian MCP for Jira/Confluence; prefer GitHub MCP for branch/commit/PR.
- When writing unit tests (implementation or verify), follow skill `verify-unit-test`.
- When generating phase artifacts, follow skill `agent-output`.
